[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715582952","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103905#issuecomment-2715582952","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103905","id":2715582952,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6h3IHo","user":{"login":"CreatedBySeb","id":11736217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzM2MjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11736217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb","html_url":"https://github.com/CreatedBySeb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T20:04:35Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T20:04:35Z","body":"To add to this bug, if you use `@export_multiline` on a typed dictionary `Dictionary[String, String]`, then you get a multiline input field that appears to be a representation of the dictionary and is non-functional (any keyboard input is immediately reverted, presumably because it is invalid).\n\n<img width=\"1792\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/60183b65-33e0-4bac-a950-150ab72a208d\" />","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715582952/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2722579600","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103905#issuecomment-2722579600","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103905","id":2722579600,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iR0SQ","user":{"login":"CreatedBySeb","id":11736217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzM2MjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11736217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb","html_url":"https://github.com/CreatedBySeb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T20:08:50Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T20:08:50Z","body":"Update on the second problem, the property seems to instead have a type of `STRING` when having the `@export_multiline` annotation, rather than `DICTIONARY` as would be expected given the type annotation of the exported variable is `Dictionary[String, String]`.\n\nSince this issue isn't present if the type hint is only `Dictionary`, my guess is there is some special handling for a plain `Dictionary` in `@export_multiline` that is preventing the bug from occurring there, but it isn't handling a typed dictionary. An issue with this handling logic down the line may also be part of the cause of the originally reported issue.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2722579600/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2722689752","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103905#issuecomment-2722689752","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103905","id":2722689752,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iSPLY","user":{"login":"CreatedBySeb","id":11736217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzM2MjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11736217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb","html_url":"https://github.com/CreatedBySeb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T21:05:19Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T21:06:30Z","body":"Found the problem for the typed Dictionary handling:\n\nThis code sets the `export_type` to the dictionary key type (though Array also seems to have similar handling but does not have the same issues):\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/701505eb4ff698434cba540381dbccdd48de8bb0/modules/gdscript/gdscript_parser.cpp#L4502-L4508\n\nBut then the code for handling `@export_multiline` only checks if the `export_type.builtin_type` is `Variant::Dictionary`, it doesn't use the `is_dict` helper variable set in the typed dictionary handling code:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/701505eb4ff698434cba540381dbccdd48de8bb0/modules/gdscript/gdscript_parser.cpp#L4516-L4528\n\nIf I add `|| is_dict` to that condition in the `@export_multiline` handler, then it behaves the same as the untyped dictionary (which is at least useable, if not really correct since it doesn't enforce the types like `@export` would, will have to come back to this later).\n\nA separate problem now, is that `@export_multiline` will accept `Dictionary[String, float]` even though it wouldn't accept `float`, so I have also added a check now that the value type of a typed dictionary is `String`. \n\nNow time to continue on to solving the original problem of fixing the multiline string editor.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2722689752/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2722709532","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103905#issuecomment-2722709532","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103905","id":2722709532,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iSUAc","user":{"login":"CreatedBySeb","id":11736217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzM2MjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11736217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb","html_url":"https://github.com/CreatedBySeb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T21:16:28Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T21:16:28Z","body":"Actually, I looked more at how Array was working since it didn't seem to need this additional help and noticed that the logic which creates the type hints for the Array is right at the end of the function before it returns\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/701505eb4ff698434cba540381dbccdd48de8bb0/modules/gdscript/gdscript_parser.cpp#L4717-L4727\n\nBut the comparable logic for Dictionary (which looks very complex) is within the branch for handling `@export` only, so it won't be applied to other annotations\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/701505eb4ff698434cba540381dbccdd48de8bb0/modules/gdscript/gdscript_parser.cpp#L4604-L4686\n\nIf I undo my previous fix of adding `|| is_dict` (but leave the check to ensure Dictionary value types are String since we still want to enforce that), then the typed dictionaries behave similarly between the `@export` and `@export_multiline`, and we don't have the issue I mentioned before. I also get a multiline input, albeit for the key which is probably not what most people will have in mind. Time to go see if I can fix that, and get it working for the generic dictionary along the way.\n\n<img width=\"1792\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ca005530-df03-4490-8bf4-a6e2265688bc\" />","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2722709532/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2722810377","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103905#issuecomment-2722810377","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103905","id":2722810377,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iSsoJ","user":{"login":"CreatedBySeb","id":11736217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzM2MjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11736217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb","html_url":"https://github.com/CreatedBySeb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T22:20:16Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T22:20:16Z","body":"Got a solution that gets us to what I imagine the expected experience would be (multiline for value not for key). Essentially at the start of the typed dictionary handling, I check if the hint is multiline and if it is then I skip adding the hint text for the key and instead apply it later. I'm a little unsure about overwriting the value hint, in case it can be set to something else that should be respected, but this does achieve the desired result so we can see if there's any feedback on implementation on the PR.\n\n<img width=\"1792\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/840396a3-791f-4199-a935-665e0f83fc1e\" />\n\nSince we have the typed Dictionaries working, one way we can fix the regular dictionaries is by inferring the value type to be `String` when `@export_multiline` is present. This seems like a pretty good solution, since the editor only allows you to put strings in this field now, but you could still put some other type in as a value programmatically if we didn't infer the value type to be `String`. I attempted to try and get a result of `Dictionary[Variant, String]` as the inferred value, but wasn't able to get that working, it was instead coming out as `Dictionary[String, String]`, which I didn't expect. I'm assuming this is because Variant is not a valid option for the key if the value is typed. Might be able to get some more feedback on this in the PR as well.\n\n<img width=\"1792\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7e7d91ba-10df-4193-8fb6-0150a968ad01\" />\n\nDraft PR with initial fixes: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104091 Will probably continue to look at this to try and find better solutions for typed and untyped dictionaries in general, since this has become interesting.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2722810377/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3505579026","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103905#issuecomment-3505579026","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103905","id":3505579026,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Q8uQS","user":{"login":"SXijka","id":112123559,"node_id":"U_kgDOBq7epw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112123559?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SXijka","html_url":"https://github.com/SXijka","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SXijka/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SXijka/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SXijka/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SXijka/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SXijka/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SXijka/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SXijka/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SXijka/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SXijka/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-08T01:47:09Z","updated_at":"2025-11-08T01:47:09Z","body":"This problem still exists in v4.5.1 stable, @export_multiline doesn't work for typed Dictionary, somehow @export_custom(PROPERTY_HINT_TYPE_STRING, \"4:;4/18:\") works.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3505579026/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4199209853","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103905#issuecomment-4199209853","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103905","id":4199209853,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc76Stt9","user":{"login":"Loregret","id":31369647,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMzY5NjQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31369647?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Loregret","html_url":"https://github.com/Loregret","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Loregret/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Loregret/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Loregret/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Loregret/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Loregret/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Loregret/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Loregret/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Loregret/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Loregret/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-07T13:13:03Z","updated_at":"2026-04-07T13:13:03Z","body":"I confirm that @export_multiline doesn't work with Dictionaries in 4.6.1 stable.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4199209853/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]